  "evidence": "The constructive degree-one Chebotarev argument and the Hilbert class field application were traced through their written source calls. The quadratic example and the bound for higher absolute residue degree were verified separately.",
  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "DOP-01",
      "chapter": "inputs",
      "title": "A Frobenius condition compatible with prime absolute norm",
      "anchor": "inputs-prime-crossing",
      "statement": "Given a finite Galois extension L/K, a target g∈Gal(L/K), and finitely many excluded primes of K, there is an absolute degree-one prime P of K outside them, unramified in L/K, and an arithmetic Frobenius at a place over P whose restriction is exactly g.",
      "hypotheses": "K is a number field. L/K is finite Galois. The exclusions are finitely many prime ideals of K. The crossing argument uses an auxiliary prime ℓ with [L:K] dividing ℓ−1 and Φ_ℓ irreducible over L. The prime-distribution input for the crossing field uses nonvanishing at one for nontrivial norm characters.",
      "definitions": [
        "absolute residue degree",
        "arithmetic Frobenius",
        "auxiliary cyclotomic extension",
        "fixed field of the cyclic subgroup generated by the adjusted lift",
        "absolute norm of a prime ideal"
      ],
